CORRECTION: this commit message misstates the toolchain versions.

The message says AGP 8.5.2 -> 8.13.2 with Kotlin at 2.0.20. The tree
this commit actually contains is:

    AGP                        9.3.1   (was 8.5.2)
    Kotlin android + compose   2.2.10  (was 2.0.20)
    Gradle wrapper             9.5.0
    Compose BOM                2024.06.00 (unchanged)
    Gradle daemon JDK          21
    Kotlin jvmTarget           17 (unchanged)

The build files were being edited concurrently by another session
while this commit was being prepared; 'git add -A' staged a newer
state than the one the message describes.

The code is correct and verified: 'gradlew clean assembleDebug'
passes locally, and PR #17 added a CI job that builds this tree
green on a clean ubuntu-latest runner. Only the message was wrong.

Note also that android.newDsl=false in gradle.properties is
load-bearing under AGP 9 -- the build fails without it.
